/**
 * @namespace SNE
 * @brief Defines the top-level namespace for Signum Engine.
 *
 * Contains all engine systems, platform abstractions, rendering backends, and
 * supporting infrastructure implemented by Signum Engine.
 */

/**
 * @namespace SNE::Engine
 * @brief Contains the core runtime systems of Signum Engine.
 *
 * Organizes the engine's application lifecycle, platform integration,
 * rendering infrastructure, diagnostics, and other runtime subsystems beneath
 * a shared engine-level namespace.
 */

/**
 * @namespace SNE::Engine::Core
 * @brief Contains engine-wide runtime coordination and core infrastructure.
 *
 * Provides systems responsible for coordinating the top-level engine lifetime
 * and other functionality shared across engine subsystems.
 *
 * Core systems should remain independent of backend-specific implementation
 * details except where they coordinate explicitly owned engine resources.
 */

/**
 * @namespace SNE::Engine::Core::Error
 * @brief Provides Signum Engine's structured error and diagnostic system.
 *
 * Defines engine error codes, subsystem classification, native API error
 * information, structured EngineError exceptions, and diagnostic formatting
 * and output facilities used across engine subsystems.
 *
 * The namespace provides the common error representation into which lower-level
 * platform and rendering APIs can translate their native failure information.
 */

/**
 * @namespace SNE::Engine::Platform
 * @brief Provides platform and window-system integration for Signum Engine.
 *
 * Contains abstractions over platform-facing libraries and resources, including
 * process-wide GLFW lifetime management, native window ownership, event
 * processing, and related platform functionality.
 *
 * Platform resources are kept separate from renderer-specific systems so the
 * engine's windowing and operating-system integration remain independently
 * structured.
 */

/**
 * @namespace SNE::Engine::Platform::Error
 * @brief Provides platform-specific error integration for Signum Engine.
 *
 * Contains adapters that capture failures reported by platform libraries and
 * translate them into the engine's shared error representation.
 *
 * Platform-specific error handling belongs here when it interprets or converts
 * native platform-library error state rather than defining engine-wide error
 * policy.
 */

/**
 * @namespace SNE::Engine::Renderer
 * @brief Contains rendering systems and graphics-backend infrastructure.
 *
 * Organizes renderer-facing abstractions and backend implementations used to
 * establish and operate Signum Engine's graphics systems.
 *
 * Backend-specific APIs are contained in nested namespaces so higher-level
 * renderer architecture can remain separated from implementation details of a
 * particular graphics API.
 */

/**
 * @namespace SNE::Engine::Renderer::Vulkan
 * @brief Contains the Vulkan rendering backend for Signum Engine.
 *
 * Provides Vulkan instance and surface ownership, physical-device discovery
 * and selection, device capability inspection, queue-family discovery and
 * planning, logical-device creation, extension policy, Vulkan result handling,
 * and related backend infrastructure.
 *
 * The Vulkan backend separates hardware capability discovery from engine
 * policy and resource creation so supported hardware capabilities, selected
 * features, queue requirements, and owned Vulkan resources remain distinct
 * architectural concerns.
 */
